type
  TdxFixtureDigest* = object
    ## One pinned fixture, its size and its digest, as DATA.
    ##
    ## The gate walks this table and checks every row against the
    ## constant of that name before reading any of them. A comment
    ## recording a digest is a comment; this is a list a loop can be
    ## defeated by dropping a row from, which is why the gate asserts its
    ## LENGTH as well as its contents.
    ##
    ## "Every row" is load-bearing and was not always true: the gate
    ## checked five of these rows and left the rest as a record that
    ## nothing compared to anything, so corrupting a row's digest —
    ## including the vendor root's — did not turn it red. The gate now
    ## pins each row by name and asserts the coverage in BOTH
    ## directions, so a row that is not checked, and a check for a row
    ## that is not here, each fail.
    name*: string
    sha256*: string
    bytes*: int

